  "worked_solution": "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (-5{t}^{4}+2t+2)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{t}^{5}+{t}^{2}+2t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(0)=-8.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8 & =-(0)^{5}+(0)^{2}+2(0)+C \\\\ -8 & =0+C \\\\ C & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=-{t}^{5}+{t}^{2}+2t-8.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=2\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =-(2)^{5}+(2)^{2}+2(2)-8 \\\\  & =-32+4+4-8 \\\\  & =-32\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $32\\,\\text{m/s}.$",
